Found during k90 (worker), reproduced with GitSource directly. GitSource.run passes {...process.env} to git, including GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE, GIT_INDEX_FILE (and the other repo-local vars). With GIT_DIR exported (skilletor run from a git hook, `git rebase -x`, tooling that exports it), a first resolve added `origin` to THAT repository and moved its HEAD to the source commit (fetch + reset --hard in the wrong repo). The k90 GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES does not help. Also check probe.ts (ls-remote) and any other git spawn (hooks.ts/engine.ts `-C` calls, gitignore.ts ls-files – those run in the user project on purpose; decide whether they should honour GIT_DIR or not). Fix: for cache runs, drop every variable `git rev-parse --local-env-vars` lists (GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE, GIT_INDEX_FILE, GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY, GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES, GIT_COMMON_DIR, GIT_PREFIX, GIT_NAMESPACE, GIT_CONFIG, GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS, GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY_n/VALUE_n, GIT_SHALLOW_FILE, GIT_GRAFT_FILE, GIT_REPLACE_REF_BASE, GIT_IMPLICIT_WORK_TREE, GIT_INTERNAL_SUPER_PREFIX …); decide about GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS/GIT_CONFIG_COUNT (may carry auth/proxy settings the user relies on for fetch) and say why. Tests: GIT_DIR/GIT_WORK_TREE pointing at a victim repo during resolve → victim untouched (remotes, HEAD, files), cache resolved normally.

